.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_STORE_EXPECT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_STORE_expect ,
.Nm OSSL_STORE_supports_search ,
.Nm OSSL_STORE_find
.Nd Specify what object type is expected
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/store.h
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_STORE_expect
.Fa "OSSL_STORE_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int expected_type"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_STORE_supports_search
.Fa "OSSL_STORE_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int criterion_type"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_STORE_find
.Fa "OSSL_STORE_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "OSSL_STORE_SEARCH *search"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn OSSL_STORE_expect
helps applications filter what
.Xr OSSL_STORE_load 3
returns by specifying a
.Sy OSSL_STORE_INFO
type.
By default, no expectations on the types of objects to be loaded are
made.
.Fa expected_type
may be 0 to indicate explicitly that no expectation is made, or it may
be any of the known object types (see
.Xr OSSL_STORE_INFO 3 )
except for
.Sy OSSL_STORE_INFO_NAME .
For example, if
.Qo Li file:/foo/bar/store.pem Qc
contains several objects of different type and only certificates are
interesting, the application can simply say that it expects the type
.Sy OSSL_STORE_INFO_CERT .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_find
helps applications specify a criterion for a more fine grained search of
objects.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_supports_search
checks if the loader of the given OSSL_STORE context supports the given
search type.
See
.Xr OSSL_STORE_SEARCH 3
for information on the supported search criterion types.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_expect
and OSSL_STORE_find
.Em must
be called before the first
.Xr OSSL_STORE_load 3
of a given session, or they will fail.
.Sh NOTES
If a more elaborate filter is required by the application, a better
choice would be to use a post-processing function.
See
.Xr OSSL_STORE_open 3
for more information.
.Pp
However, some loaders may take advantage of the knowledge of an expected
type to make object retrieval more efficient, so if a single type is
expected, this method is usually preferable.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_STORE_expect
returns 1 on success, or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_supports_search
returns 1 if the criterion is supported, or 0 otherwise.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_find
returns 1 on success, or 0 on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ossl_store 7 ,
.Xr OSSL_STORE_INFO 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_STORE_SEARCH 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_STORE_load 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn OSSL_STORE_expect ,
.Fn OSSL_STORE_supports_search
and
.Fn OSSL_STORE_find
were added in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
